   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to directing the department of transportation to establish a maximum speed limit of thirty miles per hour on state route 908H, better known as \"Ocean parkway\", in the county of Kings",
    "basePrintNo": "S5170",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5170-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1620, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5170\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to directing the department of transportation to establish a\nmaximum speed limit of thirty miles per hour on state route 908H,\nbetter known as \"Ocean parkway\", in the county of Kings\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill would direct the NYS Department of Transportation to\nestablish a speed limit of 30mph on Ocean Parkway in Kings County.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of the bill adds a new subsection (a-1) to Section 1620 of\nthe vehicle and traffic law that directs the department of\ntransportation to establish a speed limit of thirty miles per hour on\nstate route nine hundred eight H, better known as \"Ocean parkway\", in\nthe county of Kings.\n\nSection 2 is the enacting clause.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nIn 2014, New York City implemented the Zero Vision initiative, which\namong other things reduced the speed limit on certain roadways. One of\nthose roadways was Ocean Parkway in Brooklyn, which was reduced from\n30mph to 25mph. Ocean Parkway runs throughout central and southern\nBrooklyn and is heavily trafficked because there are no parallel roads\nof similar capacity.\n\nWhile reducing the speed limit on roadways is a useful tool to\nincrease pedestrian safety, Ocean Parkway is a 6 lane major roadway.\nThe speed limit reduction has had the unintended consequence of\nsignificantly increasing traffic congestion. The increased traffic has\nled to drivers choosing to use narrower residential streets causing\nnew safety concerns and congestion in neighborhoods. Local residents\nhave complained of the increase in drivers on local roads as they\nattempt to avoid Ocean Parkway.\n\nReducing speed limits to 25mph on roads across the City, particularly\nin residential areas, has had a positive impact on pedestrian safety.\nOn the other hand, major thoroughfares like Ocean Parkway, need to be\nrestored to 30mph to ensure that the high volumes of traffic on those\nroads move as efficiently as possible.\n\nThis legislation would authorize the New York State Department of\nTransportation to increase the speed limit on Ocean Parkway back to\n30mph in an effort to alleviate traffic congestion on nearby\nresidential side streets.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the thirtieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
